# Run Tests Before Every Commit

Before creating any `git commit`, always run the full test suite for every component that has changes staged.

## Test commands by component

| Changed files | Command | Working directory |
|---|---|---|
| `tools/shader_port/**` | `dart test` | `tools/shader_port/` |
| `RenderDll/XRenderMetal/test/*.cpp` | `clang++ -std=c++17 -o <name> <file>.cpp && ./<name>` | `RenderDll/XRenderMetal/test/` |
| `RenderDll/XRenderMetal/**` (shader/PSO changes) | `clang++ -std=c++17 -framework Metal -framework Foundation -framework CoreFoundation -o generated_pso_tests GeneratedPSOTests.mm && ./generated_pso_tests` | `RenderDll/XRenderMetal/test/` |

## Rules

- All tests must pass (exit code 0) before the commit is created.
- If any test fails, fix the failure first, then re-run the suite, then commit.
- Never use `--no-verify` to skip hooks unless the user explicitly requests it.

## Examples

```bash
# Dart shader toolchain changes
cd tools/shader_port && dart test

# C++ renderer logic changes
cd RenderDll/XRenderMetal/test
clang++ -std=c++17 -o renderer_logic_tests RendererLogicTests.cpp && ./renderer_logic_tests
clang++ -std=c++17 -o shader_pair_validation_tests ShaderPairValidationTests.cpp && ./shader_pair_validation_tests

# Generated PSO dry-run (requires Generated/ artifacts — run dart validate_migration.dart first)
cd RenderDll/XRenderMetal/test
clang++ -std=c++17 -framework Metal -framework Foundation -framework CoreFoundation \
    -o generated_pso_tests GeneratedPSOTests.mm && ./generated_pso_tests
```

## Integration smoke checklist (manual gate before shipping)

Run after any change to `RenderDll/XRenderMetal/**` or `Generated/**`:

1. Build the game binary (DEBUG mode) — zero compiler errors.
2. Launch the game — reaches the main menu without crash or assert.
3. Load a level — first frame completes; the `assert(fallbacks == 0)` in `CMetalRenderer::BeginFrame` must not fire.
4. `ValidateShaderPairs` (called once in `#if DEBUG` after `LoadGeneratedShaders`) reports 0 failures.
5. Visual check — no all-black surfaces, fog gradient visible, lighting responds to moving the light source.
